1who|n|The back, or top of the back; a crest. ; A range of hills or mountains, or the upper part of such a range; any extended elevation between valleys. ; A raised line or strip, as of ground thrown up by a plow or left between furrows or ditches, or as on the surface of metal, cloth, or bone, etc. ; The intersection of two surface forming a salient angle, especially the angle at the top between the opposite slopes or sides of a roof or a vault. ; The highest portion of the glacis proceeding from the salient angle of the covered way.	a:1hvn,152,4~1hvn,152,4	n:1hvn,142,2~1hvn,142,2	N:1uqz,109,17~1uqz,109,17
